ts at a time; service time is a constant 5.004 hours, uptime is a steady 200.582 hours, downtime averages 45.187 hours, and operating cost runs at $7.934 per hour. On the inventory side, lens_assembly starts at 2536616 units, with a holding cost of $7.818 per unit and a 1-hour review cycle. industrial_sensor begins with 384667 units on hand. FPGA opens at 1907024 units, is reviewed every 1 hour, and has a shortage penalty of $20.264 per unit. Finished products move from Main Factory to the Logistics Center for storage and outbound flow. Demand for industrial_sensor comes from Lenovo Group, with orders arriving somewhere between 33.0 hours and 45.0 hours apart, averaging 157781.0 units with variability of 45962.0 units. Lenovo accepts a fixed 29.0-hour customer lead time, pays $270.179 per unit, settles invoices 50.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Schneider Electric buys FPGA, with demand arrivals averaging 36.0 hours and each order fixed at 3938302.0 units. Delivery to that customer takes between 15.0 hours and 24.0 hours, the selling price is $697.739 per unit, payment comes in 52.0 to 58.0 days, and unmet sales are also lost. The modeled network explicitly links CarbonSupply Co., Process Go., and MetalFab Inc. into Main Factory, then routes industrial_sensor and FPGA onward to the Logistics Center. The scenario runs for 730 hours, with the first 30 hours treated as warm-up, and 5 replications are used.

