wer_module, and resin are consumed to make solar_panel units. That step takes exactly 18.0 days per cycle. A Packaging Machine supports the operation with capacity for 1 unit at a time, a fixed service time of 0.972 days, and an operating cost of $19.424 per day. Customer demand comes from two major accounts. Samsung Electronics orders solar_panel units with arrivals averaging 59.0 days, and each order ranges from 1937855.0 units to 3980682.0 units. Delivery to Samsung takes between 11.0 days and 29.0 days, any unfilled demand is backordered, the selling price is $2730.062 per unit, and payment is received 55.0 days later. Apple Supply places orders every 39.0 days, with demand typically around 4136054.0 units and variability of about 264923.0 units. Its delivery time is a consistent 26.0 days, available stock is shipped and any remainder is lost, the sales price is $3213.803 per unit, and customer payment comes between 46.0 days and 87.0 days. The model runs over 730 days, with results collected after a warm-up period of 30 days, and 5 replications are used.

