ys to 23.0 days. A Quality Scanner supports the process with capacity for 4 units, a service time between 0.629 days and 4.39 days, and an operating cost of $2.192 per day. Reliability is not perfect: the scanner runs for an average of 277.264 days before failure and, once down, stays unavailable for exactly 25.47 days. On the demand side, Samsung Electronics buys the SoC, placing orders every 27.0 to 33.0 days and requesting between 718477.0 units and 1875032.0 units at a time. Customer lead time ranges from 15.0 days to 29.0 days. The business follows a partial backorder approach, so available units ship immediately and the remaining demand waits for replenishment. Each SoC sells at $2686.105 per unit, and Samsung Electronics pays 19.0 days after delivery. Finished SoC output moves from Assembly Hub to the Distribution Center for downstream handling.

