164 per unit, with lead time averaging 16.0 days, payment terms ranging from 12.0 days to 20.0 days, and a limit of 539610 units per delivery. Inside the Fab, one process called polishing converts gold_wire, circuit_board, and plastic_pellet into SoC, taking between 12.0 days and 27.0 days and using the Welding Station. That Welding Station has capacity for 1 unit at a time, works with a service time averaging 6.015 days, and costs $2.627 per day to run. A separate assembly step at the same Fab turns plastic_pellet, circuit_board, and gold_wire into FPGA in exactly 17.0 days. The Fab manages circuit_board, gold_wire, plastic_pellet, and SoC in one flow, and circuit_board, plastic_pellet, FPGA, and gold_wire in another, with both SoC and FPGA then sent on to the Warehouse. On the demand side, TechCorp buys SoC every 42.0 days, ordering exactly 1110494.0 units each time. Customer delivery for TechCorp takes 2.0 days, any available stock is shipped immediately and the balance is backordered, the selling price is $176.279 per unit, and payment comes 27.0 days later. HP Enterprise purchases FPGA every 28.0 days, with order sizes varying from 2678492.0 units to 3951678.0 units. Its delivery promise ranges from 9.0 days to 25.0 days, unmet demand is lost rather than backordered, the sales price is $3859.742 per unit, and receivables are collected in 8.0 days to 73.0 days. The model runs in days over a 200 day horizon with 5 replications.

