ks, and an operating cost of $12.734 per week. Reliability matters here: the Laser Cutter stays up for a consistent 170.342 weeks before failure and, when it goes down, repair time follows an exponential pattern with a mean of 12.665 weeks. On the finished goods side, the system starts with 2492299 units of camera inventory. Holding finished stock costs $5.659 per unit, shortages cost $34.708 per unit, and the camera stock position is reviewed every 1 week. Demand comes from Ross Associates, which places orders every 31.0 weeks flat. Order size ranges from 2182860.0 units to 2498856.0 units, customer delivery takes between 1.0 weeks and 9.0 weeks, and any unmet demand is backordered rather than lost. Each camera sells at $1021.823 per unit, and customer payment is received exactly 48.0 days later. The model includes PrecisionParts, GlobalComponents, NanoMaterials Inc., the Pilot Line, and the Storage Facility in one connected network, and it is evaluated over a 730-week horizon with 10 replications.

