d_wire and display_panel into smartphone in exactly 16.0 weeks. Inventory is fairly substantial: display_panel starts at 957858 units, with holding cost of $9.226 per unit, shortage cost of $35.482 per unit, and a 1 week review cadence. Finished medical_device begins at 3547582 units with holding cost of $0.735 per unit and review every 1 week, while smartphone opens at 4247368 units with holding cost of $6.656 per unit and the same 1 week review cycle. Output from the Manufacturing Site is then sent on to the Storage Facility for both medical_device and smartphone. On the demand side, Bosch Automotive buys medical_device, placing orders every 28.0 weeks, with demand typically around 4949120.0 units and variability of about 1300039.0 units. Customer delivery takes exactly 10.0 weeks, available stock ships immediately and the remainder is backordered, the selling price is $4095.975 per unit, and cash is collected 78.0 days later. ABB Industrial purchases smartphone with order arrivals averaging 16.0 weeks, volumes ranging from 1038280.0 units to 1266414.0 units, and customer lead times between 5.0 weeks and 7.0 weeks. It uses the same partial-backorder approach, sells at $3579.976 per unit, and payment comes in between 28.0 days and 43.0 days. The model runs for a horizon of 200 weeks with 10 replications.

