e Robot Arm is not perfectly reliable either: it runs for an average of 362.631 days before failure and then stays down for exactly 39.369 days, while costing $14.291 per day to operate. On the finished goods side, industrial_sensor inventory starts at 1270107 units, is reviewed every 1 day, costs $9.078 per unit to hold, and incurs a shortage cost of $18.589 per unit. Demand comes from Siemens Digital, with order arrivals somewhere between 21.0 days and 51.0 days apart, and order size centered around 2849684.0 units with variability of 795134.0 units. Customer shipments are delivered in 9.0 to 17.0 days, sold at $3008.13 per unit, and paid 15.0 days after delivery. If inventory runs short, the business uses a partial fulfillment approach: available industrial_sensor units are shipped, and any unmet remainder is lost. The model runs for a 200-day horizon with 10 replications.

