d every 1 week. Demand comes from two major customers. HP Enterprise buys FPGA, with orders arriving exponentially at an average of 35.0 weeks, and order size is normally centered around 3102951.0 units with variability of 277403.0 units. FPGA shipments to HP Enterprise take exactly 6.0 weeks, sell at $1871.931 per unit, and follow a partial-fill lost-sales approach, meaning available units ship and the remainder is lost. HP Enterprise pays exactly 37.0 days after delivery. Siemens Digital purchases SoC, with demand arrivals averaging 27.0 weeks and quantities roughly 3423804.0 units with variation of 81303.0 units. SoC orders are delivered in exactly 26.0 weeks, sold at $3880.617 per unit, and use the same partial shipment policy where any unmet balance is lost rather than backordered. Siemens Digital pays in 28.0 days. The model runs in weeks over a 200-week horizon with 1 replication.

