 resin at $326.134 per unit, typically around 7.0 days lead time, with payment due somewhere between 26.0 days and 75.0 days after delivery; transfer to the Pilot Line takes 2.0 days. Resin is reordered when inventory falls below 1754.39 units, bringing it back to 5151.47 units, and it carries a holding cost of $5.546 per unit with review every 5 days. Demand comes from two CPU customers. TechCorp places orders exactly every 54.0 days, with each request somewhere between 449898.0 units and 4628332.0 units. Delivery to TechCorp takes between 8.0 days and 13.0 days, the business sells at $4271.464 per unit, and payment comes in 9.0 days after delivery. If stock is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Broadcom Limited orders with an average interarrival time of 48.0 days, asking for between 2293699.0 units and 4007375.0 units at a time. Its customer lead time is a fixed 22.0 days, the selling price is $3846.877 per unit, and payment is received 63.0 days later; in this case, unmet demand is backordered rather than lost. Overall, the network links Memory Star, PrecisionParts, and FastChip Corp. into the Pilot Line, and then sends CPU output from the Pilot Line to the Logistics Center, with the whole system observed over a 730-day horizon across 5 replications.

