tially spaced intervals averaging 55.0 weeks, with demand centered around 626483.0 units and varying by about 41196.0 units. Delivery to Schneider Electric takes exactly 8.0 weeks, the selling price is $1968.972 per unit, and payment comes anywhere from 38.0 to 54.0 days later. If tablet is unavailable, the sale is lost. Lenovo Group buys FPGA on a steadier pattern, ordering every 44.0 weeks, with demand averaging 280221.0 units and varying by about 77115.0 units. FPGA shipments reach Lenovo Group in exactly 1.0 week, sell at $2980.226 per unit, and are paid 51.0 days after delivery. In this case, unmet demand is backordered rather than lost. The physical network is straightforward: Memory Star sends epoxy_compound to the Integration Center, PolymerSource sends glass_fiber to the Integration Center, and the Integration Center forwards both tablet and FPGA to the Logistics Center.

