 operation that converts 3 units of lithium_cell into each EV_battery in exactly 18 days, with beginning stock set at 3545244 units of EV_battery. Finished EV_battery inventory has a holding cost of $4.17 per unit, a shortage penalty of $28.785 per unit, and a very frequent 1-day review cycle, and completed batteries also move on to the Fulfillment Hub. On the demand side, Siemens Digital buys SoC with customer arrivals averaging 11 days, order sizes around 1942038.0 units on average with variability of 564886.0 units, and a fixed 16-day customer lead time. If SoC stock is short, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered. The SoC sells at $1843.133 per unit, and Siemens Digital pays between 42 days and 85 days later. Schneider Electric purchases EV_battery every 33 days flat, with demand roughly 897800.0 units and variation of 128942.0 units, and delivery takes between 10 days and 26 days. For shortages, whatever EV_battery is available is shipped and the rest of the demand is lost. The EV_battery sells at $1453.756 per unit, with payment made 29 days after delivery.

