its of sensor_array on hand, where shortages cost $35.905 per unit and stock is reviewed every 1 hour, and it also holds 3332075 units of finished FPGA inventory, with a holding cost of $2.922 per unit and a 1-hour review cycle. Completed FPGA units move from the Processing Unit to the Warehouse. On the demand side, Broadcom Limited places orders for FPGA exactly every 37.0 hours, and each order is for 4593415.0 units. Customer delivery runs between 14.0 and 15.0 hours, and the company follows a partial-fill lost-sales approach, meaning available units ship and any remaining unmet demand is lost. Each FPGA sells at $2476.679 per unit, and cash is collected between 11.0 and 75.0 days after sale. The model runs in hours over a 365-hour horizon with 10 replications.

