 step there takes exactly 28.0 weeks and converts circuit_board plus aluminum_sheet into FPGA, and the fabrication step takes exactly 1.0 week to turn solder_paste, memory_chip, circuit_board, and aluminum_sheet into solar_panel. Fab manages aluminum_sheet, circuit_board, and FPGA in the inspection flow, and it also manages aluminum_sheet, circuit_board, memory_chip, solar_panel, and solder_paste for the fabrication flow. Downstream, TechCorp buys FPGA with orders arriving every 58.0 weeks. Demand is roughly 2231647.0 units on average, varying by about 367322.0 units, and customer delivery takes between 2.0 weeks and 17.0 weeks. If stock is short, available units ship right away and the balance is backordered. The selling price is $1932.658 per unit, and cash is collected 37.0 days after delivery. Ross Associates purchases solar_panel every 14.0 weeks, with demand centered around 4472611.0 units and variability of 54487.0 units. Shipments to that customer take exactly 20.0 weeks, and the business follows a partial fulfillment approach where available units are sent and the rest of the demand is lost. Solar_panel sells at $4808.266 per unit, and customer payment comes in between 13.0 days and 29.0 days. The network itself is simple: PrecisionParts, BatteryTech, and GlassCore Ltd. feed Fab, and Fab sends both FPGA and solar_panel to the Distribution Center. The model runs for 365 weeks, with results measured after a 50-week warm-up period.

