t_board to produce laptop output, with each production cycle varying uniformly between 7.0 days and 22.0 days. On the inventory side, the factory starts with 793725 units of circuit_board on hand, reviewed every 1 day, and shortages there cost $38.957 per unit. Finished laptop stock begins at 1970792 units, is also reviewed every 1 day, and carries a holding cost of $6.553 per unit. Demand comes from Dell Technologies, which places orders for laptop every 35.0 days. Order volume is normally centered around 1354990.0 units with variability of 166601.0 units, customer lead time ranges from 13.0 days to 28.0 days, and if stock is not available the sale is lost rather than backordered. The selling price is $4862.971 per unit, and customer payment is received between 20.0 days and 54.0 days later. The model runs in days over a 730-day horizon, with the first 30 days treated as warm-up, and 10 replications are used.

