bstrate, steel_rod, EV_battery, and copper_wire inventory, and runs a cutting step that takes exactly 15.0 days to turn copper_wire, steel_rod, ceramic_substrate, and sensor_array into EV_battery output. The business starts with 2156819 units of sensor_array on hand, with a shortage penalty of $34.639 per unit and a 1-day review cadence, while finished EV_battery inventory begins at 2750752 units, incurs $6.28 per unit in holding cost, $10.422 per unit in shortage cost, and is also reviewed every 1 day. Once produced, EV_battery units move from the Processing Unit to the Warehouse. Demand comes from Dell Technologies, which places orders for EV_battery every 35.0 days flat. Order volume is typically 1610505.0 units with variability of about 151579.0 units, customer delivery lead time runs between 10.0 days and 23.0 days, and sales are lost if product is unavailable. The selling price is $751.475 per unit, and Dell Technologies pays 27.0 days after delivery. The model runs for a horizon of 365 days with 10 replications.

