This network is built around producing the SoC for Infineon Technologies, with Memory Star, FastChip Corp., and MetalFab Inc. feeding the operation and the finished SoC moving from the Pilot Line to the Storage Facility before customer fulfillment. The raw material mix is carbon_fiber, epoxy_compound, and gold_wire, and there is also an in-house fabricated component called sensor_array. Each sensor_array uses 5 units of epoxy_compound, 4 units of gold_wire, and 4 units of carbon_fiber. Each SoC then consumes 2 units of sensor_array, plus another 2 units of epoxy_compound, 4 units of gold_wire, and 1 unit of carbon_fiber in the molding step at the Pilot Line. That manufacturing operation runs on a fixed 21.0 weeks cycle, and the Pilot Line manages inventory for gold_wire, epoxy_compound, sensor_array, SoC, and carbon_fiber. Carbon_fiber is sourced from Memory Star under a min-max replenishment approach, with orders triggered below 4521.19 units and raised to 13843.25 units. Supply from Memory Star has an exponential lead time averaging 6.0 weeks, the purchase cost is $251.089 per unit, and payment is made between 42.0 days and 67.0 days after delivery. Epoxy_compound comes from FastChip Corp. and is replenished on a regular schedule in lots averaging 75339.0 units, varying by about 3380.0 units, with arrivals anywhere from 16.0 weeks to 22.0 weeks. Its carrying cost is $9.425 per unit, shortage cost is $33.964 per unit, and stock is reviewed every 2 weeks. FastChip Corp. delivers in exactly 7.0 weeks, charges $131.339 per unit, and offers payment terms between 37.0 days and 43.0 days. Gold_wire is purchased from MetalFab Inc. using another threshold-based policy, reordering below 3528.4 units and restoring inventory to 10830.98 units. MetalFab ships in a consistent 24.0 weeks, charges $22.49 per unit, allows payment between 13.0 days and 88.0 days, and can supply up to 231350 units per order. Gold_wire holding cost is $5.817 per unit and it is reviewed every 2 weeks. Inside the operation, sensor_array starts with 1668329 units on hand, with a holding cost of $6.578 per unit, a shortage penalty of $1.315 per unit, and a 1 week review cycle. Finished SoC inventory begins at 4833837 units, carries a holding cost of $6.174 per unit, and is also reviewed every 1 week. Customer orders from Infineon Technologies arrive somewhere between 14.0 weeks and 39.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 2935494.0 units to 4307156.0 units per order. Delivery to the customer takes exactly 12.0 weeks. The sales policy is partial fulfillment, meaning available SoC units are shipped and any unmet balance is lost rather than backordered. The SoC sells at $1766.47 per unit, and customer payment comes in 86.0 days after delivery. The model runs over a 200 week horizon, with results measured after a 30 week warm-up period, and it is replicated 10 times.

