1 day, while smartphone begins with 963576 units, carries at $0.199 per unit, faces a shortage cost of $38.239 per unit, and is likewise reviewed every 1 day. Customer demand is substantial. Infineon Technologies buys GPU, placing orders every 37.0 days, with demand varying uniformly between 2200698.0 units and 2293828.0 units per order cycle. GPU orders are delivered in 20.0 days, sold at $652.926 per unit, and under shortages Plant A ships available units immediately and backorders the remainder; customer payment comes 38.0 days later. ABB Industrial purchases smartphone every 33.0 days, demanding exactly 2594022.0 units each time. Delivery to ABB Industrial takes between 4.0 days and 24.0 days, the selling price is $4610.173 per unit, and any unmet volume is fully backordered until stock becomes available, with payment received 14.0 days after delivery. In terms of physical flow, MegaSupply, ElectroParts, and Process Go. all feed Plant A, and Plant A then sends both GPU and smartphone to Regional Depot. The model runs over a 730-day horizon, with results collected after a 50-day warm-up period and evaluated across 5 replications.

