s, and it costs $15.116 per day to operate. Customer demand is sizable. Samsung Electronics places EV_battery orders every 27.0 days, with order quantities varying between 1007858.0 units and 4932842.0 units. Shipments to Samsung take exactly 5.0 days, the selling price is $2156.019 per unit, and payment comes in 44.0 to 53.0 days. If inventory is short, available units are shipped and the rest of the demand is lost. Lenovo Group buys solar_panel every 19.0 days, with demand centered around 1850550.0 units and varying by about 445572.0 units. Their delivery lead time is 10.0 days, the sales price is $821.409 per unit, and payment arrives in 20.0 to 63.0 days; if stock is unavailable, those sales are lost outright. Across the network, BatteryTech, FastChip Corp., and MetalFab Inc. all feed the Pilot Line, and both EV_battery and solar_panel then flow from the Pilot Line to the Regional Depot. The model is run over a 100-day horizon with 1 replication.

