ts of power_module, 4923365 units of medical_device, and 1029444 units of EV_battery. Finished goods move from Fab to Regional Depot for both medical_device and EV_battery. On the demand side, NXP Semiconductors buys medical_device, placing orders every 24.0 weeks flat, with demand ranging from 1079286.0 units to 2457435.0 units per order. Customer delivery expectations run between 7.0 weeks and 21.0 weeks, the selling price is $1975.783 per unit, and payment is received 53.0 days after delivery. If stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. TechCorp purchases EV_battery with order arrivals averaging 24.0 weeks, order size between 2800855.0 units and 3687644.0 units, a fixed customer lead time of 22.0 weeks, and a selling price of $1389.944 per unit. Its accounts are settled between 46.0 days and 72.0 days after delivery, and any unmet demand is backordered rather than lost. The model runs over a 365-week horizon, with results collected after a 50-week warm-up period and 5 replications.

