s a holding cost of $7.326 per unit and is checked every 1 hour. The network also includes a CNC Machine resource with capacity for 3 units at a time, a fixed service time of 8.944 hours, and an operating cost of $12.73 per hour. On the demand side, Schneider Electric orders GPU every 28.0 hours, with order sizes ranging from 1394427.0 units to 2908342.0 units. Customer delivery is a consistent 5.0 hours, the selling price is $3222.94 per unit, and payment comes in 10.0 to 35.0 days later; if stock is short, available units are shipped and the rest of the sale is lost. ABB Industrial buys laptop every 15.0 hours, with demand typically around 3911403.0 units and variability of about 436540.0 units. Laptop orders are delivered in 11.0 to 20.0 hours, sell for $4897.207 per unit, and are paid 85.0 days after receipt, with any unmet demand backordered until inventory is available. The modeled network links GlobalComponents, SiliconWorks, and PrecisionParts to Advanced Fab, and then moves both GPU and laptop from Advanced Fab to the Distribution Center. The scenario runs for 730 hours, with results collected after a 50-hour warm-up period, using 1 replication.

