le is $9.934 per unit, shortage cost is $43.467 per unit, and review happens every 1 day. Camera inventory carries at $3.723 per unit with a shortage penalty of $31.353 per unit and a 1-day review cycle. SoC is held at $3.945 per unit, with shortage cost of $20.759 per unit and the same 1-day review. On the demand side, Schneider Electric buys camera, with customer orders arriving exponentially with a mean of 11.0 days and a fixed order size of 2495301.0 units. Delivery to Schneider Electric takes between 11.0 and 29.0 days, the selling price is $3601.6 per unit, and payment is received 67.0 days later. If camera is unavailable, the sale is lost. Broadcom Limited purchases SoC, with orders showing up on average every 27.0 days and quantities ranging from 2150407.0 to 3108856.0 units. Its requested lead time is between 7.0 and 9.0 days, the product sells at $2589.368 per unit, and cash comes in after 61.0 days. For SoC, available units ship immediately and any remaining demand is backordered. The network links FastChip Corp., PolymerSource, and CarbonSupply Co. to the Pilot Line, and then moves both camera and SoC from the Pilot Line to the Regional Depot. The model runs for 730 days, with results collected after a 30-day warm-up period, across 10 replications.

