ame_structure, 4645054 units of medical_device, and 4111230 units of CPU. Frame_structure has a holding cost of $6.599 per unit and is checked every 1 day. Medical_device carries $1.93 per unit in holding cost, a shortage cost of $0.993 per unit, and a 1-day review cadence. CPU is more expensive to carry and miss, with holding at $7.746 per unit, shortage cost at $39.732 per unit, and reviews every 1 day. Customer demand comes from two very different buyers. NXP Semiconductors orders medical_device every 18.0 days, with demand roughly 2241495.0 units on average and variability of 665380.0 units; shipments reach the customer in 5.0 days, the selling price is $3065.173 per unit, customer payment comes between 30.0 days and 46.0 days, and under the partial lost-sales rule the business ships what is available and loses the remainder. Apple Supply buys CPU every 54.0 days, with demand around 101193.0 units and variability of 10547.0 units; delivery to the customer takes 21.0 days, the unit price is $2957.448, payment is received between 41.0 days and 45.0 days, and any unmet volume is backordered until stock becomes available. The model runs for a 200-day horizon with 1 replication, so all timings are expressed in days.

