ant manages heat_sink, medical_device, ceramic_substrate, and copper_wire inventory in the first flow, and heat_sink, SoC, and ceramic_substrate in the second. Starting stock is quite large: 1958149 units of heat_sink, 112790 units of medical_device, and 657131 units of SoC. Heat_sink inventory is reviewed every 1 week, costs $1.453 per unit to hold, and incurs $27.016 per unit when short. Medical_device is also reviewed every 1 week, with holding cost of $5.176 per unit and shortage cost of $3.441 per unit. SoC is reviewed every 1 week and has a shortage penalty of $8.126 per unit. Finished goods move from Advanced Fab to the Distribution Center for both medical_device and SoC. Customer demand comes from Samsung Electronics for medical_device and NXP Semiconductors for SoC. Samsung orders arrive with an average spacing of 52.0 weeks, with order sizes between 2322456.0 units and 4698464.0 units, and expects delivery in 6.0 to 27.0 weeks. The medical_device sells at $1800.023 per unit, Samsung pays exactly 19.0 days after delivery, and if stock is short, available units are shipped while the remainder is lost. NXP Semiconductors buys SoC with demand arriving on average every 11.0 weeks, in quantities from 94289.0 units to 3771883.0 units, and the promised delivery time is a fixed 24.0 weeks. SoC sells at $4373.648 per unit, NXP pays between 52.0 days and 79.0 days, and shortages are handled the same way: whatever is available ships, and the rest is lost. The model runs for a horizon of 100 weeks with 5 replications.

