ours, and an operating cost of $1.698 per hour. That machine stays up for 275.713 hours at a time and, when it fails, is down for an exponentially distributed average of 16.466 hours. Finished laptops start with 4429131 units on hand, incur $6.109 per unit in holding cost, and are reviewed every 1 hour. Tablets begin with 4771346 units in inventory, have a shortage cost of $19.769 per unit, and are also reviewed every 1 hour. Customer demand is substantial: Samsung Electronics orders laptops with arrivals between 14.0 hours and 28.0 hours, requesting between 2413378.0 units and 4573686.0 units per order. Those laptop orders are delivered in 17.0 hours to 21.0 hours, any unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $3281.957 per unit, and payment comes 71.0 days after delivery. TechCorp buys tablets on an exponential pattern averaging 47.0 hours between orders, with order sizes from 1399749.0 units to 2597800.0 units. Tablet shipments take exactly 29.0 hours, available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost, the selling price is $1329.023 per unit, and customers pay 51.0 days later. Once produced, laptops move from Production Center to Regional Depot and tablets move from Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs over a horizon of 200 hours with 10 replications.

