wntime averages 41.945 weeks, and running it costs $11.851 per week. The testing step itself takes anywhere from 1.0 week to 17.0 weeks. Finished goods inventory starts with 2714732 units of smartphone on hand, with a holding cost of $5.935 per unit, a shortage cost of $10.118 per unit, and daily-style attention translated here as a 1 week review rhythm. On the demand side, Lenovo Group places smartphone orders every 24.0 weeks, with order sizes ranging from 1541052.0 units to 2728508.0 units. Customer lead time for Lenovo Group is 17.0 weeks, the selling price is $1018.619 per unit, payment comes 24.0 weeks later, and if stock is short the business ships what it can and loses the rest. Sony Electronics behaves differently: orders arrive with an average spacing of 42.0 weeks, each order is exactly 3318699.0 units, delivery to that customer takes 2.0 weeks, the selling price is $2379.297 per unit, and payment is received between 44.0 weeks and 84.0 weeks after shipment; any unmet demand is backordered. The model runs for a horizon of 730 weeks, with 10 replications.

