 taking between 4.0 days and 9.0 days. On-hand stock starts very high, with 3169122 units of heat_sink and 4802155 units of SoC already available. Heat_sink carrying cost is $1.332 per unit, with a shortage cost of $37.814 per unit and a 1 day review interval; SoC holding cost is $8.266 per unit, shortage cost is $6.073 per unit, and it is also reviewed every 1 day. Demand comes from NXP Semiconductors, which places orders for SoC every 31.0 days to 53.0 days, with each order fixed at 4548302.0 units. Customer lead time is exactly 24.0 days, and the business follows a partial backorder approach, meaning available units ship right away and the remainder waits until stock is replenished. The selling price is $4303.169 per unit, and customer payment is received between 25.0 days and 77.0 days. The model runs for a 100 day horizon, with results collected after a warm-up period of 50 days.

