tyle monitoring translated here as a 1 week review interval. Customer demand comes from Samsung Electronics and HP Enterprise. Samsung Electronics places FPGA orders at intervals between 13.0 weeks and 36.0 weeks, with order sizes ranging from 2594638.0 to 4931288.0 units. Its promised fulfillment time is 23.0 weeks, the selling price is $2138.101 per unit, payment is received 87.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is simply lost. HP Enterprise orders FPGA every 51.0 weeks, with demand centered around 1785406.0 units and varying by about 320630.0 units. Its customer lead time is 4.0 weeks, the sales price is $4570.747 per unit, payment comes between 14.0 days and 66.0 days, and any unmet quantity is backordered until supply catches up. Structurally, all three suppliers feed the Fab, and FPGA output then moves from the Fab to the Regional Depot. The model runs in weeks over a 365-week horizon, with 10 replications.

