tart with 2591941 units in stock, with holding cost of $8.199 per unit, shortage cost of $37.906 per unit, and inventory review every 1 hour. Solar_panel begins with 1225547 units on hand. Customer demand for cameras comes from Schneider Electric, with orders arriving at an average interval of 33.0 hours and demand roughly 1863674.0 units, varying by 177621.0 units. Camera orders are delivered in exactly 1.0 hour, any shortfall is backordered, the selling price is $4363.33 per unit, and Schneider Electric pays 37.0 hours after delivery. Apple Supply buys the solar_panel, placing orders every 11.0 hours, with demand centered around 1448939.0 units and varying by 195349.0 units. Delivery to Apple Supply takes between 11.0 and 24.0 hours, available stock is shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered, and the selling price is $2900.287 per unit with payment due after 14.0 hours. In network terms, BatteryTech, ChipCo, and NanoMaterials Inc. feed Assembly Hub, and both camera and solar_panel then move on to Distribution Center. The model runs for 200 hours with 1 replication.

