ry and copper_wire inventory. There, the polishing step turns copper_wire into EV_battery units in a cycle ranging from 12 days to 22 days. Beginning inventory for EV_battery is 1243755 units, with a shortage cost of $49.328 per unit and daily review every 1 day, and completed EV_battery units are also sent on to the Warehouse. On the demand side, Lenovo Group buys camera units every 20 days, with demand centered around 1627643.0 units and varying by about 474547.0 units. Customer deliveries for camera take 24 days, any unmet volume is backordered, the selling price is $596.401 per unit, and cash is collected 26 days after delivery. TechCorp orders EV_battery units every 35 days, with demand averaging 4948568.0 units and fluctuation of about 439254.0 units. Their delivery lead time ranges from 11 days to 28 days, shortages are also backordered, the sales price is $1990.563 per unit, and payment arrives 27 days after shipment. The model runs for 100 days, with results taken after a 30-day warm-up period, using 1 replication.

