ne costs $7.988 per week. The factory also runs an assembly step for medical_device using solder_paste and power_module, with processing time varying between 12.0 weeks and 29.0 weeks. On the demand side, Siemens Digital buys FPGA, placing orders somewhere between every 31.0 weeks and 43.0 weeks, with order size ranging from 1405305.0 units to 4462136.0 units. Customer deliveries take between 7.0 weeks and 27.0 weeks, the selling price is $1467.969 per unit, and payment is received between 19.0 days and 22.0 days after shipment; if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. Samsung Electronics purchases medical_device, ordering between every 27.0 weeks and 51.0 weeks in a fixed quantity of 715523.0 units. That product is delivered in exactly 19.0 weeks, sold at $3387.676 per unit, and paid for in 24.0 to 78.0 days; available units ship immediately and any remaining demand is backordered. Material flows are straightforward: solder_paste moves from NanoMaterials Inc. to Main Factory, memory_chip moves from MegaSupply to Main Factory, and both FPGA and medical_device are transferred from Main Factory to Storage Facility. The model runs over a 200-week horizon with 1 replication.

