mewhere between 1.0 and 13.0 hours, charges $52.432 per unit, and is paid 88.0 days after delivery. Finished goods inventory starts high, with 2490889 units of EV_battery and 3682688 units of solar_panel on hand. Customer demand is also substantial: Apple Supply places EV_battery orders every 16.0 hours, with order sizes between 1962703.0 and 4722714.0 units, expects delivery in exactly 8.0 hours, and follows a partial backorder approach where available units ship immediately and the balance waits; those batteries sell at $2651.735 per unit, and customer payment comes between 7.0 and 19.0 days later. NXP Semiconductors buys solar_panel on a 29.0 to 55.0 hour order cycle, with demand centered around 2173870.0 units and varying by about 224870.0 units, delivery taking between 12.0 and 17.0 hours; this account uses full backordering, so unmet demand is queued, and the selling price is $268.696 per unit with payment arriving 89.0 days after shipment. In terms of physical flow, GlassCore Ltd., GlobalComponents, and SiliconWorks feed the Manufacturing Site, EV_battery moves from Manufacturing Site to Regional Depot, and solar_panel moves from Advanced Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs over a 500-hour horizon, with the first 50 hours treated as warm-up, and includes 10 replications.

