naging drone, resin, and silicon_wafer inventory. On the finished goods side, laptop inventory starts at 3763009 units, with holding cost of $9.692 per unit, shortage cost of $22.25 per unit, and a 1-week review cadence. Drone inventory opens at 647936 units, is reviewed every 1 week, and has a holding cost of $8.869 per unit. Demand for laptops comes from Dell Technologies every 34.0 weeks, with each order fixed at 879750.0 units. Customer delivery takes 16.0 weeks, the business sells laptops at $4911.869 per unit, and Dell pays 29.0 days after receipt. If stock is short, available units ship right away and the balance is backordered. Sony Electronics buys drones, with order arrivals anywhere from 16.0 weeks to 58.0 weeks and demand fixed at 3942664.0 units per order. Drone shipments take 25.0 weeks to reach the customer, sell at $2532.534 per unit, and payment comes 8.0 days later. In this case, unmet drone demand is lost if inventory is not available. The model runs for a 500-week horizon, with results collected after a 30-week warm-up period, across 10 replications.

