 cutting step turns resin, copper_wire, and aluminum_sheet into smartphone, with each production cycle taking between 16.0 days and 22.0 days. On the finished goods side, starting inventory is 2159421 units of FPGA and 4731189 units of smartphone. Smartphone stock is reviewed every 1 day, and any shortage there carries a penalty of $34.59 per unit. Outbound demand is split between two customers. Dell Technologies buys FPGA, with orders arriving at an average interval of 32.0 days and a fixed order size of 3556710.0 units. Delivery to Dell takes exactly 7.0 days, the item sells at $2773.03 per unit, payment comes 39.0 days later, and if inventory runs short, available units ship immediately while the balance is backordered. Infineon Technologies purchases smartphone, with demand arriving on average every 57.0 days in fixed quantities of 3987053.0 units. Customer lead time ranges from 4.0 days to 9.0 days, the selling price is $2140.744 per unit, payment is received in exactly 42.0 days, and all unmet demand is fully backordered. In terms of network flow, GlobalComponents, PolymerSource, and MetalFab Inc. all feed the Integration Center with raw materials, and both FPGA and smartphone then move from the Integration Center to the Fulfillment Hub for downstream fulfillment.

