6562.0 units; deliveries to this customer take exactly 17.0 days, the selling price is $2319.431 per unit, payment comes between 49.0 days and 81.0 days after delivery, and under shortages the business ships what is available and loses the rest. Apple Supply also buys router units, ordering every 35.0 days flat, with demand centered around 792692.0 units and variability of 82985.0 units; its delivery lead time ranges from 8.0 days to 14.0 days, the selling price is $1570.807 per unit, payment arrives in 14.0 days to 60.0 days, and any unmet balance after partial shipment is backordered. The modeled network explicitly links GlobalComponents, CarbonSupply Co., and ElectroParts to Production Center, and sends completed router units from Production Center to Warehouse. The scenario runs over 200 days, with results collected after a warm-up period of 50 days, across 5 replications.

