sts $16.979 per day. Integration Center manages both carbon_fiber and smartphone inventory. At Manufacturing Site, the coating operation turns aluminum_sheet into tablet in a cycle ranging from 3.0 days to 29.0 days, and this site manages aluminum_sheet and tablet stock. Finished smartphones and tablets are then sent on to Storage Facility. On the inventory side, smartphone begins with 1972816 units on hand, is reviewed every 1 day, and incurs a holding cost of $3.507 per unit. Tablet starts with 46189 units, is also reviewed every 1 day, and has a shortage cost of $4.384 per unit. Customer demand comes from two major accounts. Apple Supply buys smartphone, placing orders between 10.0 days and 32.0 days apart, with demand centered around 1712157.0 units and varying by about 256260.0 units. Delivery to that customer takes between 16.0 days and 19.0 days, the selling price is $4939.932 per unit, payment comes between 25.0 days and 41.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Dell Technologies purchases tablet on a fixed 31.0-day cycle, ordering exactly 4716100.0 units each time. Its delivery time is exactly 3.0 days, the tablet sells at $2431.833 per unit, payment arrives 64.0 days later, and this account also follows a lost-sales policy. The model runs for 730 days, with results collected after a 50-day warm-up period, using 1 replication.

