1 week. The site also runs an Assembly Line with capacity for 3 units, a fixed service time of 6.645 weeks, operating cost of $19.778 per week, and a failure pattern of 239.167 weeks of uptime followed by 12.19 weeks of downtime. On the demand side, Apple Supply buys SoC, placing orders every 39.0 weeks with demand centered around 3487224.0 units and varying by about 531966.0 units. Shipments to Apple Supply take 7.0 weeks, any shortfall is backordered, the selling price is $1501.962 per unit, and payment is received 81.0 days later. TechCorp purchases drone, ordering every 29.0 weeks for a fixed 1830875.0 units, with delivery taking 21.0 weeks. For that account, available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost, and the drone sells at $2005.59 per unit with customer payment arriving between 35.0 days and 54.0 days. In terms of physical flow, PolymerSource and CarbonSupply Co. feed the Processing Unit, and both SoC and drone move from the Processing Unit into the Storage Facility. The model runs for a 100 week horizon, with results collected after a 30 week warm-up period.

