epoxy_compound and power_module into EV_battery in a fixed 2.0 weeks per cycle, and a cutting step that converts glass_fiber into SoC in exactly 5.0 weeks per cycle. The site also uses a Conveyor Belt resource with capacity for 3 units, a consistent 5.033-week service time, and an operating cost of $6.341 per week. Material flow is straightforward: Memory Star, GlassCore Ltd., and CarbonSupply Co. all ship raw materials to Pilot Line, and Pilot Line sends both EV_battery and SoC to the Fulfillment Hub. Demand comes from two customers. ABB Industrial buys EV_battery, placing orders somewhere between every 13.0 weeks and 49.0 weeks, with order sizes between 12265.0 units and 4989967.0 units. Customer delivery takes between 8.0 weeks and 20.0 weeks, the selling price is $1248.941 per unit, payment arrives 50.0 days after delivery, and if stock is short the business ships what it can and loses the remainder. Bosch Automotive purchases SoC on a regular 49.0-week cycle, with demand centered around 2634799.0 units and varying by about 559203.0 units. Its delivery lead time ranges from 11.0 weeks to 15.0 weeks, the price is $786.227 per unit, payment comes between 38.0 days and 72.0 days later, and shortages are also handled by partial shipment with the unfilled balance lost. The model runs over a 200-week horizon with 5 replications.

