rs payment terms somewhere between 39.0 days and 74.0 days. On the internal stock side, the business starts with 2537057 units of display_panel and 1548430 units of industrial_sensor on hand. Finished goods are monitored very tightly, with a 1-hour review cycle, a holding cost of $3.462 per unit, and a shortage penalty of $27.169 per unit. Customer demand comes from Sony Electronics and TechCorp. Sony Electronics places orders for industrial_sensor at intervals between 25.0 hours and 57.0 hours, with demand ranging from 2751066.0 units to 4569944.0 units per order cycle. Delivery to Sony Electronics takes between 14.0 hours and 16.0 hours, the selling price is $3863.952 per unit, payment is received 41.0 days later, and if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. TechCorp, by contrast, orders every 51.0 hours flat for 2106440.0 units, expects delivery in 15.0 hours to 24.0 hours, pays $1316.676 per unit, settles invoices in 43.0 days to 70.0 days, and also follows a lost-sales arrangement when inventory is not available. The model runs in hours over a 100-hour horizon, with results collected after a warm-up period of 50 hours and 1 replication.

