PGA starts with 361498 units in stock. Keeping FPGA on hand costs $7.532 per unit, shortages cost $11.903 per unit, and the finished inventory is reviewed every 1 day. Demand comes from Apple Supply, which buys FPGA units with order arrivals following an exponential pattern averaging 59.0 days. Each request ranges uniformly from 2863970.0 units to 3978931.0 units, and customer delivery commitment falls between 8.0 days and 27.0 days. If inventory is short, available FPGA units are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered. Sales are made at $841.129 per unit, and Apple Supply pays exactly 88.0 days later. The model runs for a total of 730 days, with the first 30 days treated as warm-up, and results are based on 10 replications.

