oves from Manufacturing Site to Logistics Center, and EV_battery flows from Assembly Hub to Logistics Center. The Packaging Machine supports the operation with capacity for 4 units at a time, a consistent 0.486-hour service time, and batching enabled in lots of 42 units with a maximum wait of 19.357 hours. It is not perfectly reliable: uptime is exponentially distributed with a mean of 217.698 hours, downtime averages 8.387 hours, and it costs $12.794 per hour to run. On the finished goods side, SoC starts with 4573108 units in stock, has a holding cost of $5.916 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 hour. EV_battery begins with 4917111 units, carries a holding cost of $0.321 per unit, and is also reviewed every 1 hour. ABB Industrial buys SoC, placing orders with exponentially distributed interarrival times averaging 57.0 hours. Order size is typically 3658785.0 units with variability of about 242537.0 units, promised lead time is 17.0 hours, and the selling price is $2313.877 per unit. Under shortages, available stock is shipped and the remaining demand is lost, and ABB Industrial pays 73.0 days after receipt. Bosch Automotive purchases EV_battery with orders arriving between 35.0 and 58.0 hours apart, and quantities ranging from 331031.0 units to 3961930.0 units. Customer lead time is fixed at 22.0 hours, the sales price is $2361.105 per unit, unmet demand is lost, and payment comes in 66.0 days after delivery. The model runs for a 365-hour horizon, with results collected after a 50-hour warm-up period, using 1 replication.

