martphone orders at intervals between 25.0 days and 38.0 days, with demand averaging 86575.0 units and varying by about 6965.0 units, expects delivery in exactly 7.0 days, pays $1482.428 per unit, and settles invoices between 46.0 days and 83.0 days after delivery; if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. Broadcom Limited orders smartphones every 54.0 days flat, with demand centered around 4535161.0 units and variability of 487099.0 units, receives shipments in 29.0 days, buys at $2903.456 per unit, and pays exactly 52.0 days later, again under a lost-sales arrangement. The modeled network therefore runs supplier-to-Pilot Line flows for ceramic_substrate and resin, then sends finished smartphones from the Pilot Line to the Distribution Center, and the scenario is evaluated over a 200-day horizon with 5 replications.

