h each cycle taking between 14.0 days and 20.0 days and relying on the Packaging Machine. That Packaging Machine has capacity for 4 units at a time, works with an exponential service profile averaging 9.112 days, and batching is switched on with a batch size of 98 units and a maximum wait of 3.835 days. It also experiences breakdown behavior: uptime is a steady 248.138 days, downtime is 7.996 days flat, and operating expense runs at $1.058 per day. Demand comes from two customers. Schneider Electric places EV_battery orders arriving between 19.0 days and 59.0 days apart, each for a constant 3648285.0 units, expects delivery in 4.0 days to 6.0 days, pays $659.526 per unit, and settles invoices 14.0 days after delivery; when stock is short, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered. Ross Associates orders the same EV_battery with arrivals between 21.0 days and 32.0 days, demand fixed at 2209629.0 units, customer lead time between 11.0 days and 18.0 days, a selling price of $3373.008 per unit, and payment 32.0 days after delivery; here, unmet demand is fully backordered. The model runs for a horizon of 730 days with 5 replications.

