yment terms, and limiting deliveries to 790592 units; material from MetalFab Inc. to Pilot Line also takes an additional 7.0 to 11.0 hours to transfer. Manufacturing is centered at Pilot Line. One molding step there converts battery_pack and ceramic_substrate into CPU in exactly 4.0 hours and requires the Welding Station. That Welding Station has capacity for 5 units, works with a service time between 5.277 and 7.394 hours, and costs $13.723 per hour to run. The same Pilot Line also handles assembly of drone from glass_fiber and ceramic_substrate, with each cycle taking between 17.0 and 20.0 hours and no named resource requirement attached. Output from Pilot Line flows onward to Regional Depot for both CPU and drone. On the demand side, Ross Associates buys CPU on a fixed 54.0-hour ordering pattern, with demand centered around 3365053.0 units and varying by about 916814.0 units. Customer delivery for Ross Associates is fixed at 17.0 hours, any shortfall is backordered, the selling price is $3201.455 per unit, and payment arrives between 17.0 and 83.0 days. ABB Industrial orders drone with exponentially spaced arrivals averaging 48.0 hours, and order size ranges from 1168782.0 to 4660560.0 units. Its delivery lead time varies between 15.0 and 18.0 hours, unmet demand is also backordered, the product sells at $4099.451 per unit, and the account is paid in 21.0 days. The model runs for a horizon of 100 hours with 10 replications.

