d every 5 weeks. Production is split across two manufacturing sites. At Advanced Fab, the coating step combines silicon_wafer, microprocessor, and lithium_cell into camera, and the cycle is a consistent 2-week operation. That facility manages lithium_cell, microprocessor, camera, and silicon_wafer inventory. Processing Unit handles bonding, converting lithium_cell into SoC in exactly 7 weeks, and it manages lithium_cell and SoC stock. On the finished goods side, camera starts with 788112 units on hand, carries a holding cost of $4.181 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 week. SoC begins at 3674715 units, with holding running at $1.272 per unit and reviews also every 1 week. Customer demand is substantial. Samsung Electronics buys camera, placing orders with exponentially distributed interarrival times averaging 10 weeks; each order requests between 156997.0 units and 934749.0 units, customers expect delivery in 14 weeks to 27 weeks, the selling price is $1744.47 per unit, payment comes 19 weeks later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Bosch Automotive purchases SoC, with orders arriving anywhere from 7 weeks to 43 weeks apart and order sizes ranging from 1665322.0 units to 2510170.0 units. Its delivery promise is 22 weeks flat, the price is $1213.436 per unit, payment is received 10 weeks after delivery, and this is also a lost-sales setup. The model runs for a horizon of 730 weeks with 10 replications.

