ts of medical_device and 2732440 units of drone, and the site also manages stocks of microprocessor and epoxy_compound. On the demand side, Siemens Digital buys medical_device on a regular cadence of every 33.0 weeks, ordering exactly 3116890.0 units each time. Customer deliveries for that product take between 14.0 and 27.0 weeks, it sells at $2450.682 per unit, and the account pays in 24.0 to 71.0 days; if stock runs short, available units are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered. Dell Technologies purchases drone with orders arriving between 22.0 and 58.0 weeks apart, each for 4162897.0 units, and receives shipments in exactly 11.0 weeks. The drone sells for $2248.042 per unit, Dell Technologies pays in 78.0 days, and if inventory is unavailable, the missed demand is lost. The model runs for a 100-week horizon, with results collected after a 50-week warm-up period and 5 replications.

