ries a holding cost of $5.03 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. GPU begins with 4054019 units on hand, has a shortage cost of $3.448 per unit, and is also reviewed every 1 day. Demand for SoC comes from Dell Technologies every 32.0 days, always for 3307628.0 units, with customer deliveries taking 5.0 to 8.0 days; if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. Dell pays 7.0 to 42.0 days after delivery, and the selling price is $4470.882 per unit. GPU demand comes from Ross Associates with arrivals averaging 22.0 days, and order size is typically 2022633.0 units with variability of 327944.0 units. Ross receives product in 11.0 to 15.0 days, available units are shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered, payment lands 18.0 to 85.0 days later, and the GPU sells for $353.368 per unit. Finished SoC flows from Production Center to Regional Depot, and GPU moves from Advanced Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs in days over a 200-day horizon with 10 replications.

