 of cooling_unit, 497796 units of EV_battery, and 770886 units of laptop. Cooling_unit is reviewed every 1 hour and carries a shortage cost of $13.174 per unit. EV_battery is also reviewed every 1 hour and has a shortage penalty of $26.291 per unit. Laptop inventory is checked every 1 hour as well, with a holding cost of $1.215 per unit and a shortage cost of $26.603 per unit. On the demand side, Ross Associates buys EV_battery, placing orders every 26.0 hours with demand fixed at 2479797.0 units per order; delivery to the customer takes 18.0 hours, the business sells at $2556.385 per unit, payment comes in between 51.0 days and 66.0 days, and if stock is short, available units are shipped while the remainder of demand is lost. Siemens Digital orders laptop with arrivals averaging 31.0 hours apart, order sizes ranging from 633072.0 units to 3550773.0 units, and customer lead time varying between 8.0 hours and 28.0 hours. Laptops sell at $859.383 per unit, payment is received 73.0 days after delivery, and any unmet demand is simply lost. Material flow is straightforward: PrecisionParts sends plastic_pellet to the Production Center, BatteryTech sends copper_wire there as well, and the Production Center ships both EV_battery and laptop to the Storage Facility. The model runs for a horizon of 730 hours with 10 replications.

