s fairly reliable but not perfect: it runs for a consistent 493.201 weeks before failing, then is down for an average of 9.955 weeks before coming back online. On the finished goods side, the business starts with 1195205 units of solar_panel inventory. Demand comes from two customers. ABB Industrial places orders every 24.0 weeks, each for 374990.0 units, accepts delivery in 14.0 to 29.0 weeks, pays between 17.0 and 50.0 days later, and buys at $1345.363 per unit; if stock is short, those orders are backordered. Dell Technologies orders every 53.0 weeks, with demand centered around 1532664.0 units and varying by about 33322.0 units, expects delivery in 16.0 to 22.0 weeks, pays in 20.0 to 21.0 days, and purchases at $275.234 per unit, also under a backorder arrangement. The model runs for 500 weeks, with the first 30 weeks treated as warm-up, and includes 5 replications.

