.379 days, average downtime of 33.147 days, and an operating expense of $0.799 per day. On the demand side, Schneider Electric buys SoC, placing orders every 27.0 to 56.0 days for a fixed 2361161.0 units, expects delivery in 4.0 days, pays $4569.469 per unit, and settles invoices 58.0 days later. If SoC is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Sony Electronics purchases router, with orders arriving every 31.0 to 33.0 days and order size ranging from 1408959.0 units to 3656333.0 units. Router shipments go out in 2.0 days, sell at $234.467 per unit, and are paid in 24.0 to 38.0 days, again with partial fulfillment and the unmet balance lost. The model runs for a 100-day horizon with 5 replications.

