52 units of FPGA. The lens_assembly stock is reviewed every 1 day, and shortages there cost $38.336 per unit. Finished FPGA inventory is also checked every 1 day, with a holding cost of $7.074 per unit and a shortage cost of $5.429 per unit. On the demand side, TechCorp places FPGA orders every 18.0 days, with order volume ranging from 2004306.0 units to 2516976.0 units. Its requested delivery lead time is between 7.0 days and 28.0 days, the selling price is $3551.372 per unit, payment comes 73.0 days after delivery, and if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. Schneider Electric orders the same FPGA every 34.0 days, with demand between 2447157.0 units and 3374502.0 units. That customer expects delivery in exactly 23.0 days, pays $2466.11 per unit, settles invoices between 8.0 days and 46.0 days later, and also follows a lost sales arrangement. The model runs for a 100-day horizon with 10 replications, using days as the time basis.

