ely, reordering below 4474.01 units and restoring stock to 5995.57 units, with holding cost of $8.861 per unit, shortage cost of $38.822 per unit, and review every 27 days. Internally, display_panel inventory starts at 703764 units, with holding cost of $0.689 per unit, shortage cost of $45.754 per unit, and a 1-day review cadence. Finished industrial_sensor stock begins at 2858215 units and carries a holding cost of $6.608 per unit, also reviewed every 1 day, before moving from the Integration Center to the Regional Depot. Demand comes from two major customers. Schneider Electric places orders for industrial_sensor with arrivals between 29.0 and 41.0 days, each request fixed at 4231459.0 units, and delivery to the customer takes between 1.0 and 1.0 days, effectively 1.0 days; if inventory is unavailable, the sale is lost. Schneider Electric buys at $400.156 per unit and pays 36.0 days after delivery. Samsung Electronics also buys industrial_sensor, with order arrivals ranging from 14.0 to 46.0 days, demand fixed at 2329693.0 units, and a consistent 2.0-day customer lead time. For Samsung Electronics, available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost, and the selling price is $1074.982 per unit with payment collected after 46.0 days. The model runs in days over a 730-day horizon with 10 replications.

