 runs between 1754483.0 units and 2956908.0 units, delivery to the customer takes between 8.0 and 23.0 hours, and the business ships available units immediately while backordering the remainder. FPGA sells at $1772.272 per unit, customers pay exactly 11.0 days later, the starting FPGA inventory is 3564822 units, shortages cost $15.15 per unit, and stock is reviewed every 1 hour. Apple Supply purchases solar_panel with orders arriving between 19.0 and 37.0 hours apart, in quantities from 241748.0 units to 1442583.0 units. Their delivery time is exactly 23.0 hours, the selling price is $1697.04 per unit, and payment comes 66.0 days after delivery. For this account, available stock is shipped and the rest of the demand is lost. Solar_panel begins with 1263691 units on hand, carries a holding cost of $7.487 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 hour. The model runs for a 500-hour horizon with 1 replication.

