This network centers on smartphone production, with CarbonSupply Co., ElectroParts, and PolymerSource feeding Main Factory, and finished smartphones then moving on to the Fulfillment Hub. The raw inputs are steel_rod, aluminum_sheet, and ceramic_substrate, and the factory also builds a fabricated component called power_module before using it in final assembly. Each power_module consumes 2 units of ceramic_substrate, 4 units of aluminum_sheet, and 3 units of steel_rod. Each smartphone then requires 1 unit of power_module plus another 1 unit of steel_rod, 2 units of ceramic_substrate, and 4 units of aluminum_sheet. Steel_rod is sourced on demand, with a shortage penalty of $15.32 per unit and inventory reviewed every 21 days. Aluminum_sheet follows a min-max style replenishment rule, triggering around 4562.91 units and restoring stock to 11255.29 units; its shortage cost is $44.752 per unit and it is checked every 15 days. Ceramic_substrate is managed similarly, with a reorder point of 4412.48 units and an order-up-to level of 4649.79 units, carrying a holding cost of $8.01 per unit, a shortage cost of $42.582 per unit, and a 23-day review cycle. On the supply side, CarbonSupply Co. delivers steel_rod in exactly 15.0 days at $72.947 per unit, and payment is made between 47.0 days and 48.0 days after receipt. ElectroParts supplies aluminum_sheet with lead times ranging from 15.0 days to 28.0 days, charges $191.525 per unit, offers fixed 78.0-day payment terms, and can provide up to 206702 units per order. PolymerSource sends ceramic_substrate in a consistent 13.0-day lead time at $100.894 per unit, with payment due 35.0 days after delivery and capacity capped at 852189 units per shipment. Inside Main Factory, the coating step turns power_module, steel_rod, ceramic_substrate, and aluminum_sheet into smartphone output, and that activity takes between 1.0 days and 18.0 days. The process depends on a Quality Scanner with capacity for 2 units at a time, an exponential service pattern averaging 4.694 days, and an operating cost of $11.28 per day. Inventory at the plant starts with 2949414 units of power_module and 1293167 units of smartphone. Power_module review happens every 1 day and shortages there cost $32.151 per unit, while smartphone stock is also reviewed every 1 day and carries a holding cost of $9.689 per unit. Customer demand comes from Infineon Technologies and TechCorp. Infineon Technologies places smartphone orders anywhere from every 23.0 days to 32.0 days, with demand centered around 6741.0 units and varying by about 304.0 units. Its delivery expectation is a fixed 12.0-day lead time, the business ships available units immediately and backorders the remainder, the selling price is $4484.301 per unit, and customer payment arrives between 38.0 days and 70.0 days later. TechCorp orders every 50.0 days flat, with demand fluctuating between 2905761.0 units and 3496488.0 units. Its orders are delivered in exactly 2.0 days, available stock is shipped and the rest of the demand is lost, the sales price is $4711.646 per unit, and payment comes 36.0 days after delivery. The model runs for 200 days, with results collected after a 30-day warm-up period.

