4.645 per unit to hold, and incurs $4.758 per unit when short. Camera begins with 2005398 units, is also reviewed every 1 week, and has a holding cost of $7.028 per unit. Demand for laptop comes from Apple Supply, with orders arriving every 35.0 weeks and volume varying between 2584429.0 units and 2958873.0 units. Customer deliveries for laptop take exactly 25.0 weeks, the selling price is $1820.475 per unit, payment comes in between 26.0 days and 27.0 days, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. Camera demand comes from Dell Technologies, with order arrivals anywhere from 18.0 weeks to 57.0 weeks and demand typically around 2197999.0 units with variability of 303429.0 units. Camera shipments reach the customer in 10.0 weeks to 28.0 weeks, sell at $4217.635 per unit, and are paid in 20.0 days to 57.0 days; available stock ships immediately and the remainder is backordered. The model runs for a horizon of 730 weeks with 10 replications.

