tern averaging 18.0 weeks, and each order requests between 2855306.0 units and 3019030.0 units. Delivery to that customer takes between 13.0 weeks and 28.0 weeks, the selling price is $3614.734 per unit, and the policy is partial fulfillment—available units ship and the remainder is lost. Broadcom pays in 46.0 weeks. Sony Electronics purchases camera with orders arriving somewhere between 23.0 weeks and 43.0 weeks, each one fixed at 75864.0 units, with a customer lead time of exactly 8.0 weeks. Any shortfall is backordered rather than lost, the sales price is $4512.508 per unit, and payment comes 23.0 weeks after delivery. Overall, the model runs for 365 weeks across this setup, and 10 replications are used to test performance over time.

