here between 50.0 days and 65.0 days, holding cost is $2.536 per unit, shortage cost is $37.772 per unit, and inventory is reviewed every 18 hours. Inside the operation, frame_structure starts with 1166624 units on hand, with a holding cost of $9.374 per unit, a shortage penalty of $18.283 per unit, and a 1-hour review cycle. Finished drone inventory begins at 4045932 units, with holding cost running at $9.596 per unit and reviews every 1 hour. Production support comes from the Assembly Line, which has capacity for 5 units and a service time averaging 7.52 hours. It is not perfectly reliable: uptime lasts 276.004 hours at a stretch, followed by 25.145 hours of downtime, and operating the line costs $3.085 per hour. On the demand side, Siemens Digital buys the drone, placing orders at intervals between 18.0 hours and 57.0 hours, with order quantities between 1762081.0 units and 3537881.0 units. Customer shipments take 6.0 hours, any unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $512.3 per unit, and Siemens Digital pays 14.0 days after receipt. The model runs for a 200-hour horizon with 10 replications.

