anages aluminum_sheet, display_panel, smartphone, laptop, and ceramic_substrate, while Logistics Center acts as the downstream warehouse. At Assembly Hub, the coating step converts aluminum_sheet and display_panel into smartphone in a fixed 12.0-day cycle. A separate inspection step turns ceramic_substrate into laptop in 17.0 to 20.0 days. The site also uses an Injection Molder resource with capacity for 1 unit at a time, service averaging 7.229 days, batching enabled at 35 units, a maximum wait of 5.985 days, and an operating cost of $11.157 per day. Material flows run from SiliconWorks to Assembly Hub for aluminum_sheet, from GlassCore Ltd. to Assembly Hub for ceramic_substrate, and from GlobalComponents to Assembly Hub for aluminum_sheet, with both smartphone and laptop then moving from Assembly Hub to Logistics Center. On the demand side, Lenovo Group buys smartphone, placing orders every 26.0 to 51.0 days with demand centered around 3747025.0 units and varying by about 856385.0 units. Customer delivery for Lenovo Group takes 22.0 days, the selling price is $409.833 per unit, payment comes in 14.0 to 42.0 days, and available stock ships immediately while the remainder is backordered. Samsung Electronics purchases laptop on a fixed 40.0-day ordering pattern, with demand ranging from 1951568.0 units to 4071939.0 units. Its delivery window is 17.0 to 20.0 days, the sales price is $1164.509 per unit, payment arrives 68.0 days after delivery, and if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. The model runs for a 365-day horizon with 5 replications.

