ivery takes between 7.0 weeks and 24.0 weeks, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered, the selling price is $3964.793 per unit, and payment is received 15.0 days later. At Advanced Fab, the polishing operation turns steel_rod, copper_wire, and carbon_fiber into GPUs, taking exactly 19.0 weeks per production cycle, and that site manages copper_wire, GPU, carbon_fiber, and steel_rod inventory. GPU stock begins at 3275 units, with holding cost of $6.027 per unit, shortage cost of $4.567 per unit, and reviews every 1 week. Infineon Technologies orders GPUs every 32.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 2705529.0 units to 3411631.0 units, a consistent 14.0-week customer lead time, and a lost-sales setup if stock is unavailable. GPUs sell at $4452.124 per unit, and customer payment comes 17.0 days after delivery. Finished drones move from Fab to the Regional Depot, and GPUs move from Advanced Fab to the same Regional Depot as the downstream warehouse point.

