finished goods side, FPGA starts with 3710471 units in stock, is reviewed every 1 hour, and incurs a holding cost of $3.908 per unit. Customer demand comes from 2 buyers. Apple Supply places FPGA orders with arrivals averaging every 18.0 hours, each for exactly 1052558.0 units, and expects delivery in 6.0 to 15.0 hours. Sales to Apple Supply are priced at $3017.225 per unit, payment comes 22.0 hours later, and if stock is short, available units are shipped and the remainder is lost. Bosch Automotive orders FPGA every 37.0 hours flat, with demand centered around 4358921.0 units and varying by about 706746.0 units; its delivery promise is a consistent 23.0-hour lead time. Bosch Automotive buys at $25.635 per unit, pays 80.0 hours after delivery, and any unmet demand is simply lost. Structurally, the 3 suppliers—CarbonSupply Co., Memory Star, and NanoMaterials Inc.—feed the 2 facilities, Integration Center and Fulfillment Hub, with FPGA flowing from production to warehousing. The model runs in hours over a 365-hour horizon with 10 replications.

