t Arm. That Robot Arm has capacity for 3 units, works with an exponential service time averaging 7.837 weeks, stays up for exactly 260.082 weeks before failure, is down for 41.715 weeks when it breaks, and costs $0.063 per week to operate. Assembly Hub handles aluminum_sheet and GPU inventory and performs cutting, turning aluminum_sheet into GPU in exactly 22.0 weeks. Pilot Line manages industrial_sensor and carbon_fiber and uses inspection to convert carbon_fiber into industrial_sensor in anywhere from 13.0 weeks to 26.0 weeks. A Packaging Machine is also part of the operation with capacity for 3 units, an exponential service time averaging 8.597 weeks, uptime averaging 79.144 weeks, downtime averaging 15.854 weeks, and an operating cost of $4.571 per week. Starting stock is substantial: 2144303 units of sensor_array, 2065489 units of router, 4162226 units of GPU, and 1908023 units of industrial_sensor. The sensor_array holding cost is $2.9 per unit with review every 1 week. Router inventory carries $4.183 per unit in holding cost, a shortage penalty of $20.721 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 week. GPU starts with no stated carrying charge here, but shortage cost is $14.514 per unit with 1-week review. Industrial_sensor has a holding cost of $9.245 per unit and is also reviewed every 1 week. Finished goods from Plant A, Assembly Hub, and Pilot Line all move into the Warehouse before serving customers. On the demand side, TechCorp buys router, placing orders every 31.0 weeks flat, with demand between 2184372.0 units and 3165688.0 units per order cycle. Router deliveries to TechCorp take between 10.0 weeks and 13.0 weeks, sell at $3104.074 per unit, and use partial fulfillment with the remainder backordered; customer payment comes in 15.0 days to 23.0 days later. Dell Technologies purchases GPU, ordering anywhere from every 7.0 weeks to 26.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 2628074.0 units to 3117196.0 units. Its delivery lead time is exactly 29.0 weeks, the selling price is $2527.838 per unit, and any shortfall is partially shipped with the balance backordered; payment is received between 21.0 days and 70.0 days. Ross Associates takes industrial_sensor with exponentially spaced orders averaging 41.0 weeks, demand centered around 3637206.0 units and varying by about 872731.0 units, and delivery in 8.0 weeks to 21.0 weeks. Those units sell at $4524.271 per unit, and the business ships what it can while losing the remainder if stock is short; payment arrives between 28.0 days and 30.0 days. The modeled network explicitly links GlobalComponents, GlassCore Ltd., Memory Star, and CarbonSupply Co. to Plant A, and routes router, GPU, and industrial_sensor from Plant A, Assembly Hub, and Pilot Line into the Warehouse. The scenario runs in weeks over a 365-week horizon, with 5 replications.

