y warehouse. On the demand side, Sony Electronics buys solar_panel with orders arriving every 21.0 to 49.0 days, and each order is around 3277775.0 units with variability of 363869.0 units. Customer delivery takes exactly 9.0 days, the selling price is $2800.354 per unit, payment comes in 48.0 to 73.0 days, and if inventory is short, available units ship immediately while the rest is backordered. Broadcom Limited purchases laptop with order arrivals averaging 44.0 days, a fixed order size of 1796938.0 units, and a customer lead time of 20.0 days. Laptops sell at $2484.123 per unit, payment is received 68.0 days later, and shortages are handled by shipping what is available and losing the remainder. The operating network links CarbonSupply Co., Process Go., Memory Star, and MegaSupply to Fab, and from Fab the completed solar_panel and laptop flow into the Storage Facility. The model runs over a 730 day horizon with 10 replications.

