e varying from 3.0 days to 8.0 days. GlassCore Ltd. supplies epoxy_compound in 15.0 to 17.0 days at $186.91 per unit, with net 14.0-day payment and a 7.0-day transfer into the Manufacturing Site. CarbonSupply Co. also sends silicon_wafer, with an exponential lead time with a mean of 5.0 days, a cost of $304.135 per unit, and payment terms between 14.0 days and 68.0 days. Production is split between two manufacturing locations plus a Warehouse. The Manufacturing Site manages router, battery_pack, and epoxy_compound inventory and runs a welding step that takes battery_pack and epoxy_compound in and turns them into router units. That welding cycle ranges from 2.0 days to 26.0 days and uses the Assembly Line resource. The Assembly Line has capacity for 4 units at a time, a fixed processing time of 6.298 days, and batch operation is enabled with batches of 29 units and a maximum wait of 12.253 days. It also experiences breakdown behavior: uptime is exponential with an average of 261.489 days, downtime is exponential with an average of 46.2 days, and operating cost runs at $13.041 per day. The Assembly Hub manages solar_panel, battery_pack, epoxy_compound, and silicon_wafer inventory and performs a coating operation that combines silicon_wafer, epoxy_compound, and battery_pack into solar_panel units. That cycle runs between 14.0 days and 26.0 days. The Conveyor Belt resource in the network has capacity of 2 units, a constant service time of 8.38 days, batching turned on at 55 units, a maximum wait time of 14.84 days, and an operating cost of $7.922 per day. Output from the Manufacturing Site moves to the Warehouse as router product, and output from the Assembly Hub moves to the Warehouse as solar_panel product. On the demand side, Infineon Technologies buys router units, with orders arriving exponentially at an average of 37.0 days. Order size ranges from 12214.0 units to 1076704.0 units, promised lead time runs from 9.0 days to 26.0 days, and the business follows a parti