ply ships with an exponential lead time averaging 26.0 days, charges $405.69 per unit, and is paid in 24.0 to 32.0 days; its lane into Main Factory adds a 3.0 day transfer. ElectroParts supplies the same material in exactly 14.0 days at $417.97 per unit, allows a fixed 75.0 day payment term, and can deliver up to 775933 units. Carbon_fiber comes from GlassCore Ltd. in 13.0 days at $349.69 per unit with payment due in 40.0 to 64.0 days and a ceiling of 190965 units per order, from ChipCo with an exponential lead time averaging 4.0 days at $59.032 per unit and 51.0 to 88.0 day payment terms plus capacity of 934556 units, and from BatteryTech with an exponential lead time averaging 18.0 days at $80.002 per unit, payment in 44.0 to 68.0 days, and an added transfer time of 6.0 days. Production itself is centered at Main Factory, where the molding step turns epoxy_compound, lens_assembly, memory_chip, display_panel, and carbon_fiber into camera units on a fixed 25.0 day cycle using the Welding Station. That Welding Station has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with service times between 5.932 days and 8.574 days, runs for 445.704 days before failure on average, then stays down for an exponential 26.234 days, and costs $13.006 per day to operate. There is also an Assembly Line with capacity of 2 units, processing work in 4.702 to 6.274 days, and it runs in batches of 53 units with a maximum wait of 18.633 days; its operating cost is $6.192 per day. On the demand side, ABB Industrial orders camera units with arrivals averaging every 9.0 days, request sizes ranging from 730986.0 units to 4809089.0 units, expects delivery in 5.0 to 15.0 days, pays $4566.842 per unit, and settles invoices in 27.0 to 31.0 days; if product is unavailable, the sale is lost. Samsung Electronics places orders every 33.0 to 50.0 days for exactly 3457148.0 units, expects shipment in 1.0 day, buys at $714.84 per unit, and pays in 75.0 days; available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost. Infineon Technologies follows a similar partial-fulfillment approach, ordering every 31.0 to 44.0 days for exactly 4893000.0 units, with customer lead time between 1.0 and 9.0 days, a selling price of $2661.365 per unit, and payment due in 38.0 days. The model runs for a 100 day horizon.

