e penalty of $43.434 per unit, and a 1-week review cycle. Finished goods begin at 3077197 units of medical_device, with holding cost running at $7.601 per unit and review every 1 week. Production at Main Factory is carried out through a polishing step that consumes lens_assembly, carbon_fiber, aluminum_sheet, and frame_structure to produce medical_device. That operation uses the CNC Machine, which has capacity for 1 unit of work at a time, an exponentially distributed service time with a mean of 1.553 weeks, and batching enabled at 84 units with a maximum wait of 4.379 weeks. Running that machine costs $13.152 per week. On the demand side, Schneider Electric places orders for medical_device every 16.0 weeks, with order sizes ranging from 202138.0 to 1452729.0 units. Customer lead time is a fixed 13.0 weeks, and any unmet demand is backordered, so customers wait until stock is available. The product sells at $3966.783 per unit, and Schneider Electric pays 12.0 days after delivery. The model runs in weeks over a 500-week horizon with 10 replications.

