it, and is likewise reviewed every 1 day. Manufacturing is centered at Main Factory, which manages drone, carbon_fiber, and steel_rod in one production flow and also handles battery_pack, sensor_array, steel_rod, carbon_fiber, and router in another. The drone line is described as a polishing step that converts steel_rod and carbon_fiber into drone units, taking between 5.0 days and 13.0 days per cycle and requiring the Assembly Line. That Assembly Line has capacity for 1 unit at a time, works with an exponential service time averaging 4.778 days, batches jobs in lots of 61 units, waits up to 18.29 days to form a batch, and costs $15.094 per day to run. Router production happens through a welding step at the same Main Factory, combining sensor_array, battery_pack, steel_rod, and carbon_fiber into routers, with a cycle time ranging from 1.0 day to 14.0 days. Quality support is provided by the Quality Scanner, which has capacity for 3 units, a fixed 0.376-day processing time, batch handling enabled at 93 units, a maximum batch wait of 4.532 days, and an operating expense of $9.898 per day. Finished drones and routers then move from Main Factory to the Regional Depot. On the demand side, Samsung Electronics buys drones, placing orders at intervals uniformly between 17.0 days and 50.0 days, each order for exactly 1388660.0 units. Drone deliveries to Samsung Electronics take 17.0 days, unmet orders are backordered, the selling price is $1557.038 per unit, and customer payment arrives 60.0 days later. Apple Supply purchases routers with order arrivals following an exponential pattern averaging 53.0 days and order size fixed at 4631124.0 units. Router shipments to Apple Supply take between 14.0 days and 29.0 days, any stockout becomes a lost sale, the selling price is $2087.915 per unit, and payment comes back in between 39.0 days and 40.0 days. Structurally, the network links the suppliers Memory Star and SiliconWorks with Main Factory and the Regional Depot, and the scenario is evaluated over a 200-day horizon with 1 replication.

