st of $7.07 per unit, a shortage cost of $4.268 per unit, and is reviewed every 6 weeks. Inside the plant, solder_paste is first turned into display_panel, using 3 units of solder_paste for each panel. Aluminum_sheet is converted into motor_assembly at 5 units of aluminum_sheet per assembly, while power_module is made from 2 units of steel_rod each. The business starts with substantial in-process stock: 637367 units of display_panel, 906449 units of motor_assembly, and 2103170 units of power_module. Display_panel inventory costs $9.083 per unit to hold and is checked every 1 week. Motor_assembly is also reviewed every 1 week, and shortages there cost $31.523 per unit. Power_module has a holding cost of $1.859 per unit and the same 1 week review rhythm. Final assembly happens at Main Factory through a welding step that consumes 4 units of aluminum_sheet, 4 units of motor_assembly, 3 units of display_panel, 4 units of power_module, 2 units of solder_paste, and 3 units of steel_rod to produce 1 unit of tablet. That operation runs on a CNC Machine with capacity for 1 unit at a time, and the processing time varies uniformly between 2.0 weeks and 26.0 weeks. The CNC Machine itself has a service time between 3.678 weeks and 8.302 weeks, operates at $4.74 per week, stays up for a consistent 65.339 weeks, and when it fails, it is down for 26.598 weeks. Tablet inventory begins at 885869 units, costs $9.559 per unit to hold, and is reviewed every 1 week before being sent from Main Factory to Warehouse. On the demand side, ABB Industrial places tablet orders every 49.0 weeks, each for 3961773.0 units, expects delivery in 7.0 weeks to 15.0 weeks, pays $2437.817 per unit, settles invoices 78.0 days later, and any shortfall is backordered. Dell Technologies orders with exponentially distributed arrivals averaging 20.0 weeks, requests 1565054.0 units each time, accepts customer lead times of 12.0 weeks to 14.0 weeks, pays $2260.299 per unit, and pays between 40.0 days and 83.0 days after delivery; its orders are also backordered when stock is unavailable. Bosch Automotive orders every 50.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 1305403.0 units to 4822071.0 units, expects shipment in 11.0 weeks to 25.0 weeks, buys at $1727.105 per unit, and pays in 34.0 days; under shortage conditions, available units are shipped and the rest of the demand is lost. The model runs for a 500-week horizon, with results collected after a 30-week warm-up period, across 5 replications.

