 at $299.247 per unit with payment between 42.0 and 64.0 days; CarbonSupply Co. has an exponential lead time averaging 22.0 weeks, charges $463.795 per unit, allows 37.0 days to pay, and can supply up to 290631 units per order; NanoMaterials Inc. also averages 22.0 weeks, charges $347.895 per unit, gives 17.0-day terms, and is capped at 563474 units; GlassCore Ltd. ships in 27.0 weeks at $422.945 per unit, with 36.0-day payment terms, capacity of 949809 units, and a 1.0-week transfer to the fab. At Advanced Fab, the coating step converts lens_assembly, circuit_board, glass_fiber, and steel_rod into router output. That operation runs on a fixed 12.0-week cycle and requires the Packaging Machine, which has capacity for 2 units at a time, a constant service time of 1.538 weeks, and an operating cost of $5.126 per week. Customer demand comes from 2 major accounts. NXP Semiconductors orders router every 19.0 weeks, with demand centered around 1999774.0 units and varying by about 338149.0 units; deliveries take exactly 2.0 weeks, the price is $1115.913 per unit, payment arrives in 79.0 days, and under shortages the business ships what is available while the rest is lost. Infineon Technologies places orders with an exponential interarrival time averaging 16.0 weeks, requesting anywhere from 1665940.0 to 3255569.0 units, with customer lead time ranging from 7.0 to 28.0 weeks; routers are sold to this account at $3645.598 per unit, payment comes in 33.0 to 48.0 days, and any unmet volume is backordered until stock is available. The physical network is straightforward: all 8 suppliers feed Advanced Fab, and routers then move from Advanced Fab to Regional Depot. The model runs over a 100-week horizon with 10 replications.

