tween 34.0 weeks and 48.0 weeks after receipt. BatteryTech also supplies silicon_wafer, with lead times anywhere from 2.0 weeks to 28.0 weeks, pricing at $378.33 per unit, payment terms between 45.0 weeks and 62.0 weeks, and capacity up to 964869 units per order. GlobalComponents is the low-cost silicon_wafer source at $119.189 per unit, delivers in 3.0 weeks to 14.0 weeks, is paid exactly 44.0 weeks after delivery, and the transfer from GlobalComponents to the Fab takes 5.0 weeks. For steel_rod, Process Go. works on an exponential lead time with a mean of 10.0 weeks, charges $65.577 per unit, allows 34.0 weeks to 63.0 weeks for payment, and can supply up to 227547 units per order. PrecisionParts is slower and more expensive, averaging 13.0 weeks of lead time at $400.109 per unit, with net 26.0 weeks payment and a maximum order size of 250277 units. Inside the plant, the Fab manages heat_sink, motor_assembly, industrial_sensor, and display_panel for its assembly activity, and separately manages drone, display_panel, silicon_wafer, steel_rod, and motor_assembly for molding. The assembly step takes exactly 16.0 weeks per cycle and uses the Welding Station, transforming heat_sink, display_panel, and motor_assembly into industrial_sensor. The molding step takes 23.0 weeks flat and combines steel_rod, silicon_wafer, display_panel, and motor_assembly into drone. The Welding Station has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with an exponential service time averaging 9.739 weeks, runs for a consistent 228.12 weeks before failing, stays down for 16.451 weeks when it does, and costs $19.839 per week to operate. Finished industrial_sensor and drone output then moves from the Fab to the Storage Facility. On the customer side, NXP Semiconductors buys industrial_sensor, placing orders every 28.0 weeks to 56.0 weeks, with order quantities between 2144036.0 units and 2675423.0 units. Shipments to NXP take exactly 8.0 weeks, unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $3521.025 per unit, and payment arrives between 26.0 weeks and 72.0 weeks later. Samsung Electronics purchases drone on a faster rhythm, ordering every 14.0 weeks to 22.0 weeks, always for 4659397.0 units. Delivery to Samsung takes 22.0 weeks, available stock is shipped and the remaining demand is lost, the unit price is $2288.919, and customer payment comes in 30.0 weeks to 46.0 weeks. The model runs over a horizon of 200 weeks, with results collected after a 50-week warm-up period.

