 525852 units per order; shipments from ElectroParts to Advanced Fab take between 3.0 hours and 4.0 hours. NanoMaterials Inc. is another lithium_cell source, with lead time ranging from 2.0 hours to 22.0 hours, a unit cost of $499.346, payment terms between 13.0 days and 19.0 days, capacity of 525313 units, and transfer time to Advanced Fab between 4.0 hours and 6.0 hours. PolymerSource also sells lithium_cell, with an exponential lead time averaging 6.0 hours, a very low cost of $8.164 per unit, net 89.0 days payment, and a maximum order size of 72607 units. For solder_paste, GlassCore Ltd. delivers in 14.0 to 27.0 hours at $417.223 per unit, with 9.0-day payment terms and capacity capped at 826522 units, while FastChip Corp. supplies with an exponential lead time averaging 8.0 hours at $459.185 per unit and payment due between 15.0 days and 23.0 days. At Advanced Fab, tablet production is handled through a molding step that consumes lithium_cell and solder_paste and produces tablet output in a 7.0-hour to 24.0-hour cycle, using the Laser Cutter. That Laser Cutter has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with an exponential service time averaging 4.65 hours, and costs $6.586 per hour to run. Smartphone output is built in an assembly operation using battery_pack, power_module, and cooling_unit, with each cycle taking between 16.0 hours and 17.0 hours. FPGA production runs through a cutting step using cooling_unit and battery_pack, and that cycle ranges from 5.0 hours to 10.0 hours. Another shared asset in the system is the Quality Scanner, which has capacity for 3 units, a fixed 4.82-hour service time, and batch processing turned on at 47 units with a maximum wait of 14.812 hours. It is also failure-prone: uptime is exponentially distributed with a mean of 123.117 hours, downtime is a constant 21.849 hours, and operating cost is $14.959 per hour. Finished tablets, smartphones, and FPGA units move from Advanced Fab to the Fulfillment Hub for outbound fulfillment. On the demand side, HP Enterprise buys tablet, placing orders between every 9.0 hours and 42.0 hours for a constant 1711357.0 units, expecting delivery in exactly 20.0 hours. If stock is short, those orders are backordered, and the selling price is $4218.337 per unit, with customer payment arriving between 48.0 days and 61.0 days. Siemens Digital purchases smartphone with order arrivals averaging 56.0 hours, order sizes ranging from 2068951.0 units to 2120793.0 units, and customer lead time between 16.0 hours and 20.0 hours. This account runs on a partial shipment policy: available units are shipped and the rest is lost. Smartphones sell to Siemens Digital at $2008.269 per unit, and payment comes 29.0 days after delivery. NXP Semiconductors orders FPGA every 45.0 hours, each order being exactly 2959533.0 units, with promised delivery in 10.0 to 12.0 hours. Here the company ships what it has and backorders the remainder, and the sales price is $3763.449 per unit with payment due 14.0 days later. The full model runs for a horizon of 730 hours, with 10 replications.

