y payment terms; unfilled demand is backordered. Sony Electronics purchases GPU somewhere between every 9.0 and 13.0 weeks, with demand ranging from 2486235.0 units to 3908897.0 units, a consistent 22.0-week customer lead time, a price of $929.144 per unit, and payment in 24.0 to 77.0 days; here too, the business ships what is available and loses the remainder. In terms of physical flow, all five suppliers—FastChip Corp., BatteryTech, GlassCore Ltd., Memory Star, and CarbonSupply Co.—feed the manufacturing side, and finished SoC, solar_panel, and GPU output moves from Fab, Plant A, and Manufacturing Site into the Storage Facility. The model runs over a 200-week horizon with 5 replications.

