, cooling_unit, steel_rod, lithium_cell, carbon_fiber, and smartphone inventory in the first manufacturing stream, and lithium_cell, tablet, cooling_unit, and carbon_fiber in the second. Outbound, both smartphone and tablet flow from Main Factory to Regional Depot. Customer demand is split between two large accounts. Infineon Technologies buys smartphone, placing orders every 27.0 hours, with order sizes ranging from 561029.0 to 4366466.0 units; customer delivery lead time runs between 9.0 and 19.0 hours, the selling price is $4794.687 per unit, payment arrives 80.0 hours later, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost. NXP Semiconductors purchases tablet with exponentially spaced arrivals averaging 32.0 hours, a fixed demand of 3005340.0 units per order, a customer lead time of exactly 27.0 hours, and a selling price of $58.881 per unit; payment comes 61.0 hours after delivery, and under short supply the business ships available units while the remainder is lost. The model runs in hours over a 730-hour horizon, with 5 replications.

