.0 hours, a unit cost of $340.887, payment in 11.0 hours, and capacity of 528219 units per order. BatteryTech ships memory_chip with an exponential lead time averaging 25.0 hours, at $351.378 per unit, with payment due after 65.0 hours; its lane into Advanced Fab adds a transfer time of 2.0 to 6.0 hours. On the gold_wire side, NanoMaterials Inc. delivers in anywhere from 6.0 to 16.0 hours at $84.007 per unit and is paid 51.0 hours after delivery. MegaSupply is slower on price but constrained operationally: gold_wire lead time runs from 12.0 to 16.0 hours, the material costs $168.349 per unit, payment terms range from 27.0 to 71.0 hours, capacity is limited to 572640 units, and transfer to Advanced Fab takes between 1.0 and 9.0 hours. Memory Star supplies gold_wire in a consistent 17.0 hours, charges $239.251 per unit, allows payment in 38.0 to 53.0 hours, and can supply up to 60687 units. Production is centered at Advanced Fab, which manages gold_wire, display_panel, memory_chip, cooling_unit, heat_sink, and medical_device inventory. Its welding step converts gold_wire, memory_chip, cooling_unit, display_panel, and heat_sink into medical_device on a fixed 28.0-hour cycle, using the Laser Cutter as the required resource. That Laser Cutter has capacity for 5 units at a time, works with an exponential service time averaging 2.173 hours, and costs $1.789 per hour to run. A CNC Machine is also in the resource pool with capacity of 1 unit, exponential service time averaging 2.199 hours, batching turned on at 44 units, a maximum wait of 5.475 hours, and an operating cost of $9.038 per hour. Demand comes from two major customers. Siemens Digital places medical_device orders every 38.0 hours, always for 2140454.0 units, expects delivery in 14.0 to 17.0 hours, and buys at $3711.884 per unit; if stock is short, available units ship immediately and the rest is backordered, and payment is collected in 31.0 to 50.0 hours. Lenovo Group orders more irregularly, with arrivals following an exponential pattern averaging 22.0 hours, and order size typically around 3310430.0 units with variability of 357017.0 units. Its requested delivery window is 9.0 to 25.0 hours, the selling price is $4294.171 per unit, unmet demand is fully backordered, and customer payment comes in 52.0 to 58.0 hours. Structurally, the node setup links all 7 suppliers—CarbonSupply Co., NanoMaterials Inc., ChipCo, MegaSupply, MetalFab Inc., Memory Star, and BatteryTech—to the 2 facilities, Advanced Fab and Warehouse, with finished medical_device units flowing from Advanced Fab to Warehouse. The model runs in hours over a 730-hour horizon, with 5 replications.

