y and the balance waits; cameras sell at $2149.631 per unit and payment arrives 8.0 to 80.0 days later. HP Enterprise buys smartphone on a fixed 48.0-week cycle for exactly 3471926.0 units, accepts delivery in 13.0 to 27.0 weeks, and follows a partial-fill lost-sales rule, so whatever is available ships and the rest is lost; the selling price is $4333.57 per unit with payment in exactly 34.0 days. Broadcom Limited purchases laptop with exponentially spaced orders averaging 8.0 weeks, each for 3437602.0 units, expects fulfillment in 10.0 to 13.0 weeks, and if stock is unavailable the sale is lost entirely; laptops are sold at $120.745 per unit and collected on 23.0 to 46.0 day payment terms. Structurally, all 6 suppliers—ElectroParts, MetalFab Inc., ChipCo, Process Go., GlobalComponents, and BatteryTech—feed the Manufacturing Site, and the Manufacturing Site then sends camera, smartphone, and laptop to the Fulfillment Hub.

