arts at 3252323 units and is reviewed every 1 week, with holding cost at $0.123 per unit and shortage cost at $40.251 per unit. Cooling_unit opens at 144619 units, also on a 1-week review cadence, with holding cost of $2.363 per unit. Finished smartphone stock begins at 2069773 units, with $4.56 per unit in holding cost, $16.826 per unit in shortage cost, and review every 1 week. GPU inventory starts at 3460289 units, has a shortage penalty of $0.769 per unit, and is checked every 1 week. Tablet inventory opens at 3174122 units, with holding cost of $6.047 per unit, shortage cost of $31.725 per unit, and the same 1-week review frequency. Operationally, the Processing Unit manages smartphone, glass_fiber, cooling_unit, and epoxy_compound inventory and runs an inspection step that takes epoxy_compound, glass_fiber, and cooling_unit as inputs to produce smartphone output. That inspection cycle ranges from 16.0 weeks to 19.0 weeks and requires the Robot Arm. The Robot Arm has capacity for 1 unit at a time, works with a service time between 3.73 weeks and 6.723 weeks, and costs $9.829 per week to operate. The Manufacturing Site manages GPU, lens_assembly, epoxy_compound, and silicon_wafer, using a cutting process to turn lens_assembly, silicon_wafer, and epoxy_compound into GPUs in 16.0 weeks to 24.0 weeks. The Fab handles tablet and cooling_unit inventory, and its cutting step converts cooling_unit into tablets in exactly 25.0 weeks. Once built, smartphones move from the Processing Unit to the Logistics Center, GPUs flow from the Manufacturing Site to the Logistics Center, and tablets are sent from the Fab to the Logistics Center. Customer demand is substantial and product-specific. Ross Associates buys smartphones, placing orders every 31.0 weeks to 45.0 weeks, with order sizes between 358676.0 units and 2436327.0 units. Delivery to that customer takes 15.0 weeks to 21.0 weeks, unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $1130.999 per unit, and payment is received 18.0 days after delivery. Apple Supply purchases GPUs on a fixed 31.0-week ordering pattern, with demand centered around 1498378.0 units and varying by about 63739.0 units. GPU shipments take exactly 25.0 weeks, available stock is shipped immediately and the remainder is backordered, the sales price is $1836.872 per unit, and customer payment comes in 33.0 days to 53.0 days. Dell Technologies orders tablets every 19.0 weeks, with demand roughly 444429.0 units and variability of 31240.0 units. Tablet lead time to the customer is a consistent 18.0 weeks, partial fulfillment is allowed with the balance backordered, the unit selling price is $4737.771, and payment arrives 29.0 days after receipt. Overall, the node structure ties all 3 suppliers to all 4 facilities, while the explicit material flow sends epoxy_compound from ChipCo to the Processing Unit, silicon_wafer from PrecisionParts to the Processing Unit, and glass_fiber from NanoMaterials Inc. to the Processing Unit before finished smartphones, GPUs, and tablets are consolidated through the Logistics Center.

