uminum_sheet in a fixed 19.0 days at $11.026 per unit, with payment due 17.0 days after delivery and capacity of 915372 units. For carbon_fiber, MegaSupply delivers in 4.0 to 11.0 days, charges $116.401 per unit, gives 33.0 to 35.0 days to pay, is capped at 343179 units per delivery, and the lane into Main Factory adds a 10.0-day transfer; NanoMaterials Inc. delivers carbon_fiber in 5.0 to 21.0 days at $242.842 per unit, with payment due in 48.0 to 71.0 days and a maximum order size of 570333 units; Process Go. sends carbon_fiber in exactly 12.0 days at $238.183 per unit with net 15.0 days payment. Inventory buffers are huge in this setup: cooling_unit starts at 3571429 units, with holding cost of $8.714 per unit, shortage cost of $33.659 per unit, and daily review every 1 day; circuit_board opens at 1428018 units with shortage cost of $39.979 per unit and review every 1 day; motor_assembly begins at 2847928 units with shortage cost of $11.435 per unit and a 1-day review cycle; finished camera inventory starts at 4494972 units and carries a holding cost of $1.101 per unit with review every 1 day. Demand comes from three big customers. Schneider Electric places camera orders every 49.0 days, with order quantities between 877946.0 units and 1115222.0 units, expects delivery in 16.0 to 29.0 days, accepts backorders when stock is short, pays $1989.329 per unit, and settles invoices in 52.0 to 59.0 days. Infineon Technologies orders on a cycle ranging from 25.0 days to 54.0 days, with demand centered around 3449971.0 units and varying by about 319699.0 units, requires a consistent 28.0-day customer lead time, also works on a backorder basis, pays $4558.504 per unit, and remits payment 53.0 days after delivery. Broadcom Limited orders every 34.0 to 56.0 days, demands exactly 3977100.0 units per order, expects shipment in 5.0 days, and uses a partial-backorder arrangement where available units ship immediately and the rest wait; its selling price is $179.931 per unit and customer payment comes between 10.0 days and 36.0 days. Material flows from PolymerSource, MegaSupply, FastChip Corp., NanoMaterials Inc., GlassCore Ltd., and Process Go. into Main Factory, and completed camera units move from Main Factory to Warehouse. The model runs over a horizon of 365 days with 1 replication.

