 of $22.369 per unit, and a 1-hour review cycle, while display_panel begins at 2052871 units with holding cost of $1.319 per unit and is also checked every 1 hour. Finished laptop inventory starts at 4806456 units, carries a shortage penalty of $40.381 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 hour. For aluminum_sheet specifically, the business tracks a holding cost of $5.427 per unit, a shortage cost of $31.58 per unit, and reviews stock every 4 hours. Production takes place at the Production Center, which manages aluminum_sheet, gold_wire, display_panel, laptop, frame_structure, glass_fiber, and lens_assembly. The main step there is a testing operation that consumes aluminum_sheet, lens_assembly, gold_wire, display_panel, frame_structure, and glass_fiber to produce laptop output, and each cycle takes exactly 10.0 hours using the Robot Arm. That Robot Arm has capacity for 2 units at a time, works with a service time between 5.442 hours and 6.421 hours, and costs $9.493 per hour to operate. There is also Test Equipment on site with capacity of 4 units, service time ranging from 3.596 hours to 8.695 hours, and operating cost of $13.498 per hour; it is not perfectly reliable, staying up for an average of 283.766 hours before failure and then being down for about 24.74 hours on average. On the demand side, Broadcom Limited places laptop orders with arrivals averaging every 33.0 hours, requesting between 619959.0 units and 812492.0 units per order. Broadcom expects delivery in 17.0 to 28.0 hours, pays at $1753.207 per unit, and settles invoices in 12.0 to 29.0 days; if stock is short, available units ship immediately and the balance is backordered. NXP Semiconductors is an even larger customer, ordering on average every 25.0 hours, with demand ranging from 1043283.0 units to 4479554.0 units. Its requested lead time is tighter at 6.0 to 11.0 hours, the selling price is $4009.175 per unit, and payment comes in 20.0 to 82.0 days, again with partial shipment and the remainder backordered. The model runs in hours over a 200-hour horizon, with the first 30 hours treated as warm-up before results are counted.

