h a consistent 9.0-day supplier lead time, a unit cost of $273.014, 48.0-day payment terms, a capacity limit of 232884 units, and a 3.0-day transfer to the plant. Copper_wire inventory carries a holding cost of $7.378 per unit, a shortage penalty of $36.318 per unit, and a 6-day review cadence. Steel_rod follows a periodic replenishment pattern too, with orders fixed at 58621.0 units and arrivals every 3.0 to 21.0 days. PrecisionParts supplies it with a lead time ranging from 14.0 to 15.0 days, a price of $218.671 per unit, payment due in 48.0 to 53.0 days, and a delivery cap of 322783 units. Holding steel_rod costs $3.809 per unit, shortages cost $9.737 per unit, and planners review that stock every 2 days. On the shop floor, molding is the main production step at the Production Center, converting ceramic_substrate, gold_wire, copper_wire, cooling_unit, and steel_rod into industrial_sensor. That operation runs on a fixed 11.0-day cycle and requires the CNC Machine. The CNC Machine has capacity for 4 units, processes work in 5.279 to 7.024 days, batches are enabled at 44 units, and jobs can wait up to 18.437 days to form a batch; its operating cost is $7.268 per day. A Conveyor Belt with capacity 4 supports flow with a constant 4.345-day service time and an operating cost of $11.152 per day. For inventory positions inside the network, cooling_unit starts with 20477 units on hand, has a shortage cost of $0.828 per unit, and is reviewed every 1 day. The industrial_sensor begins with 4154003 units in stock, incurs $3.976 per unit in holding cost, $12.359 per unit in shortage cost, and is also reviewed every 1 day. Demand comes from Broadcom Limited, which places orders for industrial_sensor with arrivals averaging 23.0 days apart. Order size ranges uniformly from 2130433.0 units to 3407337.0 units, and customer delivery lead time is between 4.0 and 5.0 days. If inventory is short, available units ship immediately and the remainder is backordered. The sales side is lucrative at $1910.109 per unit, with customer payment received 24.0 days later. Finished industrial_sensor units move from the Production Center to the Regional Depot, and the whole setup is evaluated over a 730-day planning horizon with 10 replications.

