rder size of 46349 units; transfer to Advanced Fab takes between 7.0 days and 11.0 days. For memory_chip, GlobalComponents supplies at an average lead time of 23.0 days, charges $67.218 per unit, offers payment in 45.0 to 67.0 days, and can supply up to 691451 units per order; transport to Advanced Fab takes 2.0 to 5.0 days. ChipCo is another source for memory_chip, with an exponential lead time averaging 17.0 days, a unit cost of $361.23, payment in 7.0 to 47.0 days, and capacity limited to 368240 units. PolymerSource also covers memory_chip, with delivery in 4.0 to 19.0 days, a cost of $312.366 per unit, payment due in 22.0 to 63.0 days, and capacity up to 449107 units. Ceramic_substrate comes from MegaSupply and MetalFab Inc. MegaSupply ships with a consistent 22.0-day lead time, charges $232.629 per unit, has net 89.0-day payment, and can supply up to 321833 units per delivery. MetalFab Inc. offers the same material with an exponential lead time averaging 15.0 days, a price of $238.034 per unit, and payment due 14.0 days after delivery. At Advanced Fab, the molding step turns ceramic_substrate, power_module, resin, and memory_chip into medical_device units, and each run takes exactly 3.0 days using the Robot Arm. That Robot Arm has a capacity of 5 units, an exponential service time averaging 7.976 days, and operating expense of $15.296 per day. It is not perfectly reliable either: uptime is a fixed 339.515 days, followed by a fixed 34.179 days of downtime when failures occur. Finished medical_device output then moves from Advanced Fab to Storage Facility. Demand comes from two customers. HP Enterprise places orders for medical_device every 25.0 days flat, with order sizes ranging uniformly from 572114.0 units to 3876244.0 units, expects delivery in 11.0 to 17.0 days, pays between 24.0 days and 69.0 days later, and buys at $59.447 per unit; if stock is unavailable, the sale is lost. ABB Industrial orders the same product every 55.0 days, with demand centered around 4326964.0 units and varying by about 996388.0 units, accepts delivery in 9.0 to 22.0 days, pays in 35.0 to 49.0 days, and purchases at $4260.124 per unit, again under a lost-sales policy. The model runs for 365 days, with results collected after a warm-up period of 50 days, across 1 replication.

