r receipt, or from MetalFab Inc., which delivers in exactly 9.0 hours, charges $150.681 per unit, and offers payment terms anywhere from 32.0 to 89.0 days. Epoxy_compound follows a periodic replenishment pattern of 51054.0 hours, with arrivals varying from 4.0 to 14.0 hours; it costs $9.766 per unit to hold and is reviewed every 5 hours. PrecisionParts supplies it with lead times between 5.0 and 20.0 hours, a unit cost of $77.161, 30.0-day payment terms, and a maximum delivery size of 936220 units, while GlassCore Ltd. provides a very steady 4.0-hour lead time, charges $70.006 per unit, and gets paid between 53.0 and 84.0 days later. Copper_wire is bought on demand, and Process Go. supports that flow with an exponential lead time averaging 9.0 hours, a cost of $13.55 per unit, payment due 27.0 days after delivery, and capacity capped at 662315 units per order. Inside Advanced Fab, the starting stock of heat_sink is 329505 units with a holding cost of $2.636 per unit and review every 1 hour. Sensor_array begins at 4619348 units, is reviewed every 1 hour, and carries a shortage penalty of $14.985 per unit. Motor_assembly starts at 3684472 units, also reviewed every 1 hour, with a shortage cost of $18.435 per unit. The EV_battery line at Advanced Fab manages epoxy_compound, sensor_array, heat_sink, motor_assembly, EV_battery, and copper_wire, using a bonding step that takes exactly 23.0 hours and requires the Quality Scanner. That scanner has a capacity of 4 units, a service time fixed at 3.249 hours, operates at $8.155 per hour, stays up for 451.886 hours at a time, and when it fails it is down for 30.559 hours. Tablet production happens at the same site through a fabrication step using motor_assembly and aluminum_sheet, with each run taking between 1.0 and 5.0 hours. SoC production uses a cutting operation on copper_wire, microprocessor, epoxy_compound, and sensor_array, and that step runs in a narrow 14.0 to 15.0 hour window. Finished goods then move from Advanced Fab to the Warehouse. On the inventory side, EV_battery opens with 1228681 units in stock, a holding cost of $1.325 per unit, and 1-hour reviews; tablet starts at 4952675 units with $0.389 per unit holding cost and the same 1-hour review rhythm; and SoC begins at 2816914 units, with holding cost of $4.542 per unit, shortage cost of $13.966 per unit, and review every 1 hour. Customer demand is sizable. Apple Supply buys EV_battery, placing orders between every 25.0 and 54.0 hours for between 2630021.0 and 4844878.0 units, expects delivery in 13.0 to 14.0 hours, accepts a full backorder arrangement when stock is short, pays $3517.906 per unit, and settles invoices 47.0 days later. Schneider Electric orders tablet every 46.0 hours, with demand centered around 1093287.0 units and varying by about 259019.0 units; deliveries take 8.0 to 14.0 hours, available stock ships immediately and the rest is backordered, the selling price is $1255.856 per unit, and payment arrives between 18.0 and 70.0 days. Siemens Digital buys SoC on an exponential order pattern averaging 46.0 hours, with demand roughly 3365942.0 units and variability of 84118.0 units; the promised lead time is exactly 14.0 hours, shortages are handled by shipping what is available and backordering the balance, the price is $790.867 per unit, and customer payment comes 22.0 days after delivery. The model runs for a total of 500 hours, with the first 30 hours treated as warm-up, and it is repeated 10 times.

